                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18aab7a0-605f-32df-a021-1333208dd2ad",
                        "entry_id": "f89d4bd4-3fb2-3b25-b318-4096c278fe42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient feudal state of China that existed between 778 and 207 BC."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "922b2063-1b18-3477-a8da-4146aac653f2",
                        "entry_id": "f89d4bd4-3fb2-3b25-b318-4096c278fe42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The first imperial dynasty of China, lasting from 221 to 207 BC."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd613e3c-36b0-485d-b43f-988d3298b4d2",
                                "sense_id": "922b2063-1b18-3477-a8da-4146aac653f2",
                                "text": "The youth of China, deeply concerned with the future of their country, began to question everything and re-evaluate everything. What had been considered valuable became worthless, and what had been regarded as worthless became priceless. The more they examined, the more doubtful they became. This inquisitive approach shook the ancient political system, which had been handed down with little modification from the Chin Dynasty more than twenty centuries before. The new generation cried, \"Democracy.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e32456b7-5f60-41a3-a175-7e199b417315",
                                "sense_id": "922b2063-1b18-3477-a8da-4146aac653f2",
                                "text": "Sian was the captial of the Cin Dynasty(221B.C. - 201B.C.), which built the Great Wall of China. The city is now known for archeological finds, such as the clay soldiers, horses and arms buried with the emperor of the Cin Dynasty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a30dac16-1cb5-465b-b905-651b4eb9c42a",
                                "sense_id": "922b2063-1b18-3477-a8da-4146aac653f2",
                                "text": "Until 1974, the name Qin Shihuangdi (221-210 B.C.) was essentially known to specialists through the annals of Sima Qian, official historian to the Han dynasty (206 B.C.-220 A.D.). The Han overthrew the Qin dynasty founded by the First Emperor and this might call for reservations concerning his objectivity. Yet Sima, who wrote a century after the facts, was well informed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "baec3acd-a5cd-44c1-9af4-ee533d06a80d",
                                "sense_id": "922b2063-1b18-3477-a8da-4146aac653f2",
                                "text": "The highlight of every Chinese New Year meal with the family is when the \"hongbao\", red envelopes filled with brand new banknotes, are handed out at the end. The tradition goes back to the Qin dynasty (221 - 206 BC) when hongbao were given to children to protect them from evil spirits."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05167ed6-b57b-36b6-b24a-0e365d4c899d",
                        "entry_id": "f89d4bd4-3fb2-3b25-b318-4096c278fe42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A surname from Chinese."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "38947c5e-4e5a-4d4d-acee-43090bc93413",
                                "sense_id": "05167ed6-b57b-36b6-b24a-0e365d4c899d",
                                "text": "Qin and Meng applied for permission to have a child from authorities in Huangshan city in eastern Anhui province, where her residency is registered, said the officer, who gave only his surname, also Qin."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
